From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Log the x86 fault context when no debugger is attached.

UnhandledExceptionFilter ends a process with no debugger after printing a
one-line message, which does not say where a 32-bit guest faulted. On i386
call log_exception_context32() first, so the PW_EXCEPTION32 register, stack
and code-page records reach the log before the process ends.
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
index 579b70d542..916c4d6d6a 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
@@ -965,6 +965,9 @@ LONG WINAPI UnhandledExceptionFilter( EXCEPTION_POINTERS *epointers )
         {
             char buffer[256];
 
+#ifdef __i386__
+            log_exception_context32( epointers );
+#endif
             format_exception_msg( epointers, buffer, sizeof(buffer) );
             MESSAGE( "wine: %s (thread %04lx), no debugger, ending the process\n",
                      buffer, GetCurrentThreadId() );
